### Refund Requests
<p class="note--message">For non mid-term refunds, see <a href="https://apolloikb.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/37316526683533-Evaluate-process-refund-exceptions">Evaluate & Process Refund Exceptions</a></p>.
<div class="tabs">
  <ul id="tabs-nav">
    <li><a href="#rr1">Below $15k ARR</a></li>
    <li><a href="#rr2">$15K to $50K ARR</a></li>
    <li><a href="#rr3">More than $50k ARR or more than $5k refund</a></li>
  </ul>
  <div id="tabs-content">
    <div id="rr1" class="tab-content">
        <ul>
            <li>Billing may approve within their limits (See Refund Approval Matrix).</li>
            <li>Escalate to Jocel or Santiago Taborda in #ama-support-billing via the PA Billing Refund Exception Request workflow if Senior Billing approval is needed.</li>
            <li><a href="https://apolloikb.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/39671482574221-How-to-Escalate-to-Different-Teams">Escalate to Billing Ops</a> for accounts bound by contract or refunds above senior billing limits.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    <div id="rr2" class="tab-content">
      <p>Customers often reach out to Sales directly. If Support receives the request:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Loop in their account manager if they’re already part of the conversation, or;<br>
            Ping their account manager in #sales-team-support if they’re not in the Intercom conversation yet.</li>
        <li>Billing may take ownership of the ticket and open a back-office ticket if approved by sales.</li>
        <br>
        Escalate to Legal in <a href="https://apolloio.slack.com/archives/C03R6CVPPUY"></a>#gtm-customer-contracting</a> for exceptional cases.
    </ol>
    </div>
    <div id="rr3" class="tab-content">
      <p>Escalate to Sales in <a href="https://apolloio.slack.com/archives/C02JV4RBKMM">#sales-team-support</a> with request context. Their account manager will take over the conversation.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
